Architecture plan for Issues #47-#52

Context
- App: myClawTeam Official Blogs, a Next.js App Router + TypeScript editorial blog/CMS.
- Persistence: PostgreSQL through Prisma. Posts, categories, and subscribers already exist.
- Binary storage: S3-compatible object storage already handles post cover/inline images through lib/storage/object-storage.ts.
- Admin: custom HMAC cookie session, protected by proxy.ts. Admin mutations are server actions.

Module structure and file organization
1. Data/model layer
   - prisma/schema.prisma
     - Extend Post with:
       - isFeatured Boolean @default(false) mapped to is_featured if following existing snake_case convention.
       - authorName String mapped to author_name.
       - authorIntro String @db.VarChar(500) mapped to author_intro.
       - authorAvatarKey String? mapped to author_avatar_key.
     - Add a migration under prisma/migrations for the new columns.
   - prisma/seed.ts
     - Populate featured and author fields for all sample posts.
     - Ensure any sample published posts have required cover/author data after Issue #48.

2. Shared post/content helpers
   - lib/content/posts.ts
     - Keep published visibility helpers centralized.
     - Add reusable select/include shapes or helper functions only if multiple pages need the same featured/latest queries.
     - Preserve the invariant: public visibility means status PUBLISHED and publishedAt is not null.

3. Storage helpers
   - lib/storage/object-storage.ts
     - Reuse existing uploadPostImage, getSignedPostImageUrl, and deletePostImage for author avatars unless issue implementation benefits from a thin semantic wrapper such as uploadAuthorAvatar/deletePostImage alias.
     - Keep database values as relative object keys without OBJECT_STORAGE_PREFIX.
     - Delete old avatar objects when replacing/removing avatars and when deleting posts.

4. Admin editor and mutations
   - app/admin/posts/_components/post-editor-form.tsx
     - Add featured checkbox.
     - Add author name, author intro, author avatar upload, existing avatar preview/details, and remove-avatar checkbox on edit.
     - Keep cover image input and make UI communicate that cover and author fields are required only for published posts.
   - app/admin/posts/actions.ts
     - Extend PostFormValues and parsing/validation.
     - Validate authorName and authorIntro for published posts.
     - Enforce cover image for published posts, counting an existing cover as valid on edit unless remove/replace leaves none.
     - Upload avatar, clean up newly uploaded files on failure, delete replaced/removed old avatars after successful DB update.
     - Include avatar deletion in deletePost alongside cover deletion.
   - app/admin/page.tsx
     - Include featured/author data if useful for dashboard display, but avoid unnecessary UI churn unless required.

5. Public homepage and article pages
   - app/(public)/page.tsx
     - Replace current multi-section homepage with:
       - Hero using most recently published featured post.
       - Fallback hero using latest published post when no featured post exists.
       - Article card grid using signed cover URLs, title, excerpt, category, publication date, and links to /blog/[slug].
     - Resolve signed cover URLs server-side. Do not expose storage keys directly.
     - Decide what to render when no published posts exist: an empty/placeholder editorial state that keeps layout stable.
   - app/(public)/blog/[slug]/page.tsx
     - Render cover figure only if coverImageKey exists.
     - Remove fixed /images/editorial-hero.png fallback from page and JSON-LD.
     - Add author block beneath article body using signed avatar if authorAvatarKey exists, plus authorName and authorIntro.
     - Update JSON-LD author to use post.authorName and include image only when a real cover exists.

6. Retired listing routes and navigation
   - app/(public)/blog/page.tsx
   - app/(public)/blog/page/[page]/page.tsx
   - app/(public)/blog/category/[category]/page.tsx
   - app/(public)/blog/category/[category]/page/[page]/page.tsx
     - Redirect all listing/category/pagination routes to / while preserving /blog/[slug].
   - components/layout/site-header.tsx and site-footer.tsx
     - Remove links that imply a blog index/archive route.
   - app/sitemap.ts
     - Drop blog index/category/page listing URLs.
     - Keep published post detail URLs.

7. Tests
   - tests/content-visibility.test.ts
     - Update fixtures/expectations for required published fields if helper logic changes.
   - tests/admin-session.test.ts and tests/newsletter.test.ts
     - No expected changes unless shared setup changes.
   - e2e/publish-public-view.spec.ts
     - Update admin publishing flow for cover and author requirements.
     - Assert homepage hero/card grid, /blog redirect to /, detail author block, and absence of fixed fallback banner.

Dependencies between issues
- #47 is foundational: schema/migration/seed fields must land before admin/public UI relies on them.
- #48 depends on #47: admin editor/server actions parse, validate, upload, clean up, and persist the new fields.
- #49 depends on #47 and should coordinate with #48 validation: homepage uses isFeatured and required cover data for published posts.
- #50 depends on #47 and storage behavior from #48: detail page renders author block/avatar and no fixed fallback cover.
- #51 depends on #49: once homepage is the primary article discovery surface, retire listing routes and navigation/sitemap entries.
- #52 depends on all prior issues: tests should reflect the final public/admin flow.

Key design decisions
- Postgres remains the source of truth; Prisma migrations are required for model changes.
- Use existing S3-compatible object storage for covers and avatars; store only relative keys in Post rows.
- Do not introduce a separate Author model unless later requirements need reusable authors. Issue scope asks for per-post author fields.
- Keep public pages server-rendered and sign private image URLs server-side.
- Preserve published visibility semantics and add stricter publish-time validation rather than hiding malformed published posts later.
- Keep route compatibility for article details at /blog/[slug], while redirecting only index/listing/category routes.
- Avoid adding new dependencies unless needed; current stack is sufficient.
